From a0c77ac577ce00e7ec2a0eff0b4551338d8824fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 16:49:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/47] hydra: translate MaterialX noise onto the MaterialX
 noise node

The ten noise families now reach mx_noise_texture instead of being approximated
by Cycles' own noise and voronoi textures. One node covers them all, told apart
by a dimension count and a noise type, so the fixed values a mapping carries had
to learn to set an integer socket and not only a named enum.

Which output to read comes from the nodedef variant, not from what the output
feeds: ND_fractal3d_float is one scalar broadcast across the channels while
ND_fractal3d_color3 is three separate noises, so reading the destination's type
would turn every greyscale noise driving a colour into a coloured one. Hence the
paired table entries, the _float one winning on prefix length.

Also adds HD_CYCLES_DUMP_GRAPH: point it at a directory and each translated
material is written out as a .dot. Reading the graph is what settled where the
coordinates were being lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/material.cpp | 126 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 117 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

